# A custom .stow-local-ignore REPLACES stow's built-in default ignore list, so we
# must re-list the defaults we still want (README, VCS junk, etc.) alongside our
# own additions — otherwise stow would start symlinking README.md into $HOME.
#
# Patterns are Perl regexes matched against both the full path (anchored) and each
# path segment. See `man stow`, "IGNORE LISTS".

# --- our additions ---
# SETUP.md is repo documentation (the runbook), not something to plant in $HOME.
# The live Obsidian copy lives in the vault; this committed copy is read from the repo.
^/SETUP\.md$

# --- stow's usual defaults, restated ---
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
\.gitignore$
\.git$
\.gitmodules$
\.DS_Store$
